    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0194" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1936v04/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Outer Mongolia/88: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-02T18:00:00+08:00">April 2, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 2—5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>164. Embassy’s 160, April 1, 7 p.m.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d86-f1"/></p>
                <p>Tass report of April 2 under Moscow dateline states the Mongol forces repulsed
                    the attack in the region of Tomsykbulak with heavy losses, driving the
                    Japanese-Manchurian detachments back over the border.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
